title: 'Epiphany: the Paradigm Harness is "the linux of harnesses"'
summary: 'Founder: "claude code can still be the battle tested gold standard. but the Paradigm HArness that we will give a name to eventually will be the linux of harnesses that allows for extreme customization and flows". Reframes 8.0 from a layer above harnesses to a real, deeply customizable harness that interoperates with Claude Code rather than replacing it. Fourth scout (own tool family) landed: the Claude runner is implemented three times (flow, constellation, Conductor), approvals three times, scheduling 3+, five append-only ledgers, five UI shells, "session" with four meanings — the family is already a harness in pieces.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#paradigm-harness'
decisions:
  - id: P8-D2
    decision: 'Claude Code remains the battle-tested gold standard; the Paradigm Harness (name TBD) is the linux of harnesses: extreme customization and flows'
    rationale: Founder's framing. Positions the harness as a composable kernel+userland for power users rather than a Claude Code competitor.
learnings:
  - 'The founder''s own tools already form a harness in pieces: three stream-json Claude runners, three approval UIs, 3+ schedulers, five ledgers, five UI shells, four meanings of ''session''. 8.0 is consolidation into one kernel as much as invention.'
  - Linux analogy implies a small stable kernel (identity, event log, scheduler, permissions, process model) with everything else as swappable userland packages and distros.
